/P 144 0 R
/E (a Pandemic Emergency under the amended Pandemic Agreement of 2024, representing one of the first significant applications of the new Pandemic Framework. Unlike Zaire ebolavirus, which has licensed vaccines such as Ervebo, there are currently no approved vaccines or therapeutics for BDBV. The healthcare workers provided supportive care while the WHO, research institutes, and pharmaceutical companies worked on clinical trials for a vaccine and potential treatments. Furthermore, the outbreak highlighted critical surveillance gaps, with the WHO reporting a delay of approximately four weeks between the first suspected case and laboratory confirmation and challenges differentiating between similar)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
