246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 523 0 R
/E (Italy turned out to be the first epicenter of the coronavirus outbreak in Europe. There was an outbreak of cases in the Lombardy region. Hospitals faced a shortage of ICU capacity and had to allocate ICU facilities for those who were in critical condition owing to ventilators' and ICU beds' deficiency. Many healthcare professionals got infected because of the shortage of protective equipment and their long-term exposure to the disease, despite Italy having one of Europe's advanced healthcare systems.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 524 0 R
/E (The total number of deaths in America due to COVID-19 stood at about 1.2 million which was the highest number of national deaths anywhere in the world. Shortages of testing kits, poor contact tracing methods, and lack of coherent policies hampered the containment process.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 525 0 R
/E (In the wave of the Delta variant, India's healthcare witnessed an unparalleled situation where hospitals lacked oxygen, ICU beds, medicines, and even healthcare professionals. In major cities like Delhi and Mumbai, there have been cases of patients queuing up outside the hospitals since the bed availability was not sufficient. Lack of oxygen resulted in many preventable deaths due to the same reason in India, despite India's later success in large-scale vaccine production.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
