>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (framework and strengthen its egal authority, institutionalize equity making it accessible to all nations, regardless of economic status and protect the vulnerable. Ebola epidemics and Hantavirus infections are additional examples that indicate that global health security cannot depend only on the emergency response to the existing epidemics. Continuous strengthening of national health care systems through funding of disease surveillance, laboratory capacity, health workforces, research, and emergency preparedness should be prioritized in the long run. Cooperation between the Member States, WHO, and the UN becomes crucial in terms of providing timely exchange of information, equal access to vaccination, testing, treatment, and international response. Although there are some reforms such as 2024 amendments of IHR and WHO Pandemic Agreement that can become a good chance to enhance global health security, their success will ultimately depend on political commitment and financing.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
